<title>INDIA: Fake shares scare on India's National bourse - paper.</title>
<headline>Fake shares scare on India's National bourse - paper.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forged share certificates worth around 400 million rupees have been circulated on the National Stock Exchange (NSE), the Economic Times said on Thursday, quoting market sources.</p>
<p>The newspaper said exchange officials pegged the total value of the suspected fake shares at around 100-150 million rupees.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the shares had been introduced by member broker, but the exchange has not yet declared any defaulters.</p>
<p>&quot;At present it is only a suspicion. We have to see if the shares are rectified or not, before drawing conclusions,&quot; NSE's managing director R.H. Patil told the newspaper.</p>
<p>NSE officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
